# Platform-injected on deploy. Copy to .env locally if needed — never commit secrets.
# DATABASE_URL=
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=
# GROK_AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GROK_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GROK_PREVIEW_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=           From this app's OWN Google Cloud OAuth client
#                             (Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials),
#                             NOT the broker's. Used for native Google
#                             sign-in in production/local dev
#                             (src/lib/auth/server.ts's socialProviders) --
#                             the live-preview sandbox still uses the
#                             broker (GROK_AUTH_*) instead, since only that
#                             solves the preview iframe's partitioned
#                             cookies. Google Console's Authorized redirect
#                             URI must be exactly
#                             `${BETTER_AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google`.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=       Paired with GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID above. Absent
#                             entirely (not merely disabled) when either of
#                             this pair is unset -- src/lib/auth/server.ts
#                             only spreads `socialProviders.google` into the
#                             Better Auth config when both are present, so
#                             an unconfigured deploy never renders a Google
#                             button that can't actually complete a sign-in.
# XAI_API_KEY=
# SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=       The store's checkout domain (e.g.
#                             pay.kanji-ai.jp) -- src/lib/shopify-checkout.ts
#                             builds cart permalinks against this and
#                             /handoff shows it to a parent before
#                             redirecting there. No scheme, no trailing
#                             slash.
# SHOPIFY_VARIANT_BUYOUT=     The ¥9,800 permanent/buyout plan's variant id
#                             from the Shopify Admin (Products), NOT the
#                             amount and not a product id -- src/lib/shopify-
#                             plan.ts matches on this id, not on price, so an
#                             amount changing in Shopify no longer needs a
#                             matching code change.
# SHOPIFY_VARIANT_ANNUAL=     Same, for the ¥3,800 1-year pass variant.
# SHOPIFY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=     From the Shopify Admin's webhook config (or the
#                             app/custom-app's API credentials, if webhooks
#                             are registered via the Admin API) -- src/routes/
#                             api/webhooks/shopify.ts. Required at runtime --
#                             the endpoint fails closed (500) without it
#                             rather than accepting unverified deliveries.
#                             After setting it, register the three webhook
#                             topics this app handles (orders/paid, orders/
#                             cancelled, refunds/create) pointing at
#                             https://app.kanji-ai.jp/api/webhooks/shopify,
#                             send a test delivery, and confirm a
#                             billing_event row actually appears (see
#                             docs/commerce-launch-checklist.md) -- a wrong
#                             secret fails signature verification silently,
#                             with no error a parent would ever see.
